-- title:
--   Two invariant generators suffice over a field
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $\kappa$ a field and $X$ a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $\kappa$ in the sense of the project, i.e. a two-dimensional commutative formal group law $F = X.F$ over $\kappa$ together with an action of $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ by endomorphisms of the law and a series $\varpi$ with $\varpi\circ\varpi = [p]$ and $\varpi\circ a = \sigma(a)\circ\varpi$; only the law $F$ enters the statement. Let $I$ be an ideal of $\kappa[\![x_0,x_1]\!] =$ `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) κ` subject to four hypotheses: the quotient $\kappa[\![x_0,x_1]\!]/I$ is a finite-dimensional $\kappa$-module; there is $q$ with $x_i^{q} \in I$ for both $i$; every element of $I$ has vanishing constant coefficient; and $I$ is contained in the ideal generated by those $w \in I$ that are invariant, meaning that $w(F(x,y)) - w(x)$ lies in the ideal of $\kappa[\![x,y]\!]$ generated by the image of $I$ under $x_i \mapsto y_i$ (substitution of the right-hand variables). The conclusion asserts the existence of a pair $u : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to \kappa[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$ such that each $u_j$ has vanishing constant coefficient, each $u_j$ is invariant in exactly the above sense, and the ideal generated by $u_0, u_1$ equals $I$.
--
--   This is the "two generators suffice" step for finite-codimension invariant ideals of the formal plane: an ideal of $\kappa[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$ cutting out a finite subgroup scheme of the formal group $F$ and generated by invariant series can be generated by two invariant series without constant term. It is used in the construction of quotients of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules by finite subgroups, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_pair_invariant_forall_exists_coeff_sub_mem_of_isMaximal`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_pair_invariant_forall_exists_coeff_sub_mem_of_isMaximal); the proof combines a syzygy count for invariant generators with the Noetherianity of $\kappa[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$ and a bound on the number of generators of the maximal ideal of the subring they generate.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_exists_span_range_eq_of_le_span_setOf_invariant_of_field.lean

